# Project: db kind rewind (Tauri + React + Rust)

## Global Context

You are building "db kind rewind", a native macOS desktop widget that acts like a "video game save state" for local PostgreSQL databases.

The UI must be a floating, minimal widget (approx 320x480) with a dark-mode, retro VCR / hardware aesthetic. 

## AI Tooling Rule (CRITICAL)

Before writing Tauri code, always refer to the official Tauri V2 LLM documentation: https://v2.tauri.app/llms.txt

## Frontend Rules (React + TypeScript + Vanilla CSS)

- STRICTLY use vanilla CSS via CSS Modules (e.g., `ComponentName.module.css`) for all styling. 
- DO NOT use Tailwind CSS or any utility class frameworks.
- Use Framer Motion for snappy, sub-second micro-interactions (e.g., swapping a loading bar for a checkmark).
- Aesthetic: Deep dark grays/blacks, glowing VFD green or neon accents, chunky mechanical-feeling buttons. 
- UI Signifiers: Use terms like "REWIND" (to restore) and "INDEX MARK" (to register a snapshot). 

## Backend Rules (Rust)

- KEEP RUST DUMB. Do not over-engineer the Rust backend.
- Do not build complex state management in Rust. State lives in React.
- The Rust backend (`src-tauri/src/main.rs`) is ONLY a bridge to execute raw SQL queries via the `tokio-postgres` crate.
- If a Rust compiler error occurs, prioritize the simplest, most brute-force fix rather than introducing complex lifetimes or traits.
